<p>BALANCE OF PAYMENTS - Imports are already known to have risen 1.3 percent in October so exports will need to rise to stop the deficit widening from September A$1.69 billion. One unknown will be the net income deficit since the Bureau of Statistics will have new data on Q3 foreign investment to plug into its series. So far the ABS has only been estimating the net income shortfall based on past trends this could cause revisions to past deficits. The makrets are generally comfortable with the deficit at current levels and only a widening to A$2.0 billion or more would alarm.</p>
